{"nodes": [{"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_package", "label": "backend/perspective_engine package", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is one tile engine; this package does not place tiles, it prepares inputs and checks outputs. It is the backend's connection to tiles_backend/perspective_engine."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_masks_py", "label": "masks.py mask loading and validation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Refuses anything not strictly 0/255, resizes to the render size and keeps the two masks disjoint, so the clipping boundary handed to the tile engine is verbatim and unambiguous."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_render_py", "label": "render.py render_tiled_room", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assembles estimated camera, fallback VP, wall choice, the tile engine and objects-back into the engine.Result shape /generate already writes, so the new renderer needs no change in the response contract."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_compositing_py", "label": "compositing.py final strict clip", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-checks the finished image, objects included, after the tile engine's own clip - a second independent check rather than trusting the engine's clip alone."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_fallback_vp", "label": "Fallback vanishing point", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "live_scene estimates the camera from the floor's far edge and the room length, and its straight-ahead horizon is handed to the tile engine, which uses it only when it rejects its own vanishing point - a backstop, not an override."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_wall_choice", "label": "Wall choice and wall_region", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Left/right/back are the backend's room-box walls; when only some are chosen, the pixels engine._project_walls assigns to them become the tile engine's wall_region. Every wall still renders with one shared scale as in the reference, and only the chosen walls' pixels are kept."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_restore_props", "label": "engine._restore_props objects back on top", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Objects are put back over the tiles from the original photograph through their soft alpha, so no generated pixel reaches the final props."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_tiles_backend_engine", "label": "tiles_backend/perspective_engine reference tile engine", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The reference project's tile renderer, migrated unchanged, so the existing calibrated and legacy paths stay byte-identical."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_unchanged_paths", "label": "Unchanged render paths guarantee", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The calibrated room, an upload with no Clean Room run, and a job predating the floor/wall stage all still render exactly as before; the new renderer only engages when a Clean Room job_id has both masks."}, {"id": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_one_tile_engine", "label": "There is one tile engine", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This package deliberately does not place tiles - it only prepares inputs and checks outputs - so tile placement has a single implementation (tiles_backend/perspective_engine, migrated unchanged) and the backend adds only masks, a fallback VP, wall choice and the objects on top."}], "edges": [{"source": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_package", "target": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_masks_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_package", "target": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_render_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_package", "target": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_compositing_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/perspective_engine/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_render_py", "target": "backend_perspective_engine_readme_masks_py", "relati